{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"agent_message","text":"A strong hardware-specific improvement emerged: streaming the large gradient/probability/dropout arrays through the global cache while retaining the reused attention mask in the closer cache cuts representative latency by about 10–22% (and 3–4% on the largest tensors). I’m applying the same cache policy to the grouped path, then I’ll re-benchmark selection boundaries before final verification."}}
